==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|balefull}} {{qualifier|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|baleful}}, {{m|enm|balful}}, {{m|enm|baluful}}, from {{inh|en|ang|bealuful}}, which being equivalent to {{suffix|ang|bealu|ful}}. {{surf|en|bale|-ful||gloss1=evil, woe|pos=adjective}}. See {{l|en|bale}} for further etymology.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbeɪl.fəl/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-baleful.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[portend|Portending]] [[evil]]; [[ominous]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1873|author=w:James Thomson (B.V.)|title=s:The City of Dreadful Night
|passage=The street-lamps burn amid the '''baleful''' glooms,<br>Amidst the soundless solitudes immense<br>Of ranged mansions dark and still as tombs.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1936|author=Rollo Ahmed|title=The Black Art|publisher=Long|location=London|page=186|passage=According to them all sorcerers, necromancers and evil-doers were born under the '''baleful''' influence of the seventh calendic sign[.]}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1938|author=w:Xavier Herbert|title=[[w:Capricornia (novel)|Capricornia]]|location=New York|publisher=D. Appleton-Century|year_published=1943|chapter=XII|page=194|url=https://archive.org/details/capricornianovel00herb
|passage={{...}} he went off alone with his family, and, watched by the day's red '''baleful''' eye, pumped the pump-car homeward, {{...}}}}
#* '''1949''', {{w|Naomi Replansky}}, “Complaint of the Ignorant Wizard” in ''Ring Song'' (published 1952):
#*: I learned the speech of birds; now every tree<br>Screams out to me a '''baleful''' prophecy.
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Peter Sutcliffe obituary|url=https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2020/nov/13/peter-sutcliffe-obituary|work=The Guardian|author=Duncan Campbell|date=November 13 2020|passage=Few people cast a more '''baleful''' shadow over postwar Britain than {{w|Peter Sutcliffe}}, the “Yorkshire Ripper”, who has died aged 74}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|work=FT Weekend|date=2023-09-02|title=The real Rino|author=Simon Schama|section=Life & Arts|page=2|passage=In their excellent essay in The Atlantic endorsing disqualification, Luttig and Tribe remind us that the first president, in his 1796 Farewell Address, had foreseen many of the elements of this '''baleful''' disaster.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[miserable|Miserable]], [[wretched]], [[distressed]], [[suffering]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 6-2|act=III|scene=ii|line=48||passage=Thou '''balefull''' Messenger, out of my sight:}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=I|line=56|text=round he throws his '''baleful''' eyes, that witnessed huge affliction and dismay {{...}}|year=1873}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[deadly|Deadly]], [[mortal]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Romeo and Juliet|act=II|scene=iii|page=60|passage=With '''balefull''' weedes, and precious Iuiced flowers, / The earth that's Natures mother, is her Tombe,}}

